frame(firm = [1, 1], year = [2020, 2020], sales = [8, 9]).panel(unit: firm, time: year)
---
error[Z0601]: `firm` 1 is observed twice at `year` 2020
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:59
  |
1 | frame(firm = [1, 1], year = [2020, 2020], sales = [8, 9]).panel(unit: firm, time: year)
  |                                                           ^^^^^ a unit with two rows at one time
  |
  = help: a unit has one row per time: `duplicates([firm, year])` lists the repeated pairs; drop or aggregate them first

frame(firm = [1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 3], year = [2020, 2020, 2021, 2021, 2022, 2022]).panel(unit: firm, time: year)
---
error[Z0601]: `firm` 1 is observed twice at `year` 2020; 2 other pairs repeat
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:79
  |
1 | frame(firm = [1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 3], year = [2020, 2020, 2021, 2021, 2022, 2022]).panel(unit: firm, time: year)
  |                                                                               ^^^^^ a unit with two rows at one time
  |
  = help: a unit has one row per time: `duplicates([firm, year])` lists the repeated pairs; drop or aggregate them first

frame(firm = [1, NA], year = [2020, 2021]).panel(unit: firm, time: year)
---
error[Z0601]: `firm` has NA in 1 row, which a panel cannot order
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:56
  |
1 | frame(firm = [1, NA], year = [2020, 2021]).panel(unit: firm, time: year)
  |                                                        ^^^^ NA among the values
  |
  = help: `where(!is_missing(firm))` drops those rows, or `drop_missing([firm, year])`

